#: ../../guide/publishing.rst:6
msgid "Publishing and Saving Resources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/publishing.rst:9
msgid "What resources *can* be published to the network?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/publishing.rst:11
msgid ""
"Environment and Software resources are the only types of resource that "
"can currently be published and shared between EaaSI nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/publishing.rst:13
msgid ""
":term:`Content` and associated Content Environments are assumed to be "
"collection items, unique to each node/institution, and therefore "
"potentially subject to different terms of access, licensing, etc. than "
"general software copyright. Content resources therefore can not be "
"Published in the EaaSI Client, whether on their own or contained within "
"Content Environments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/publishing.rst:17
msgid "What resources *should* be published?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/publishing.rst:20
msgid ""
"Once published to the network, removing or deleting an Environment may "
"have severe technical repercussions, since users at other nodes may have "
"generated derivatives from that Environment, which would break."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/publishing.rst:23
msgid ""
"Nodes and users are advised to design and enforce local workflows for "
"publishing resources, given these technical restrictions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/publishing.rst:26
msgid ""
"When selecting resources to share with the rest of the network, EaaSI "
"users and admins can consider questions posed by the `Code of Best "
"Practices in Fair Use for Software Preservation "
"<https://www.arl.org/storage/documents/publications/2018.09.24_softwarepreservationcode.pdf>`_:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/publishing.rst:29
msgid ""
"Did you lawfully acquire your copy of the Software (and/or the software "
"included in an environment)?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/publishing.rst:30
msgid "Is the software still reasonably available in the commercial marketplace?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/publishing.rst:31
msgid ""
"Are there any limitations present in donation or acquisition agreements "
"that might preclude fair use?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/publishing.rst:32
msgid "What license(s) was the software distributed under?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/publishing.rst:34
msgid ""
"The resources and environments provided by Yale University Library will "
"hopefully provide illustrative examples for the type of content that "
"might be appropriate to share, but this will also be an ongoing, "
"collaborative conversation within the Network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/publishing.rst:40
msgid "How to publish Environments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/publishing.rst:42
msgid ""
"In a selected Private Environment's Actions menu, select \"Publish to "
"Network\":"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/publishing.rst:52
msgid "How to save published Environments to a local node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/publishing.rst:54
msgid ""
"In a selected Public Environment's Actions menu, select \"Save to My "
"Node\":"
msgstr ""

